  "description": "Bubblewrap (/usr/bin/bwrap) is a core execution engine for unprivileged containers that works as a setuid binary on kernels without user namespaces.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * bubblewrap: symlink traversal via /oldroot allows writing files outside sandbox during setup (CVE-2026-87766)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
